## What woke you

A message in #general (tp-m1) from oidc:ada@example.com:
(no words)

Files:
- farm-tomato-patch-tp-plan.png (image/png)

It is a snapshot of the farm at tomato-patch/tp-plan, zoom level 2 of 3, showing everyone's work, at night.
The view: https://lands.example/beads/garden?at=tomato-patch/tp-plan&z=2
What it framed:
- project tp-proj: tomato-patch
- plan tp-plan: Add a watering schedule
- bead tp-s1: Water the beds

Look before you answer. Fetch the files:
  gb commons file tp-m1
It prints the path of each file it writes, under commons-files/tp-m1/ in
your scratch directory:
  .../commons-files/tp-m1/farm-tomato-patch-tp-plan.png
Read each image path it prints before you answer, so you answer about the
picture, not its file name.

They sent no words. The ask: Say what you see on this part of the land and what, if anything, needs the owner.

Answer in this message's thread, not as a new post, so the picture,
the ask and your answer stay together:
  gb say --thread tp-m1 "<answer>"
If the answer is a plan, write it as duty 2 says and reply here with its id.

